#: ../../source/docs/git-interactive-rebase.rst:5
#: afe0516bf2b2441381771dac82d9ff37
msgid "Interactive Rebase: cleaning up commits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-interactive-rebase.rst:9
#: 331c18f6392c4974aa7a519ea57a21cb
msgid "This page gives a quick introduction on how to `use interactive rebase <https://help.github.com/articles/about-git-rebase/>`__ to clean up commits on your :ref:`cloned <git-clone>`.  This is often required before :ref:`submitting a pull request to the main ArduPilot repo <submitting-patches-back-to-master>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-interactive-rebase.rst:12
#: 0fa9170131f64326adaf40abf5dc7889
msgid "These instructions give the command line instructions but the same operations can be done using Git GUI editors including `SourceTree <https://www.atlassian.com/blog/sourcetree/interactive-rebase-sourcetree>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-interactive-rebase.rst:16
#: eb4a750dc3b246bf8e893e08dad74b8a
msgid "Steps in an interactive rebase"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-interactive-rebase.rst:18
#: d9a5acc6c9e449df9fa25c3de0ba097e
msgid "open up a terminal and cd to your :ref:`clone's <git-clone>` directory, checkout the :ref:`branch <git-branch>` you wish to cleanup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-interactive-rebase.rst:25
#: d3ef3e339a1643c7b11a287178d2d690
msgid "use the git rebase -i command with the range of commits to be modified.  For example to modify any of the last 10 commits:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-interactive-rebase.rst:31
#: 8bf238f45c9f41eea61b922dafbe5495
msgid "in the terminal that pops up (see top image on this page) find the commits you wish to modify and replace their ``pick`` with one of the following letters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-interactive-rebase.rst:33
#: 2b4f140b55ed4b878468d9c513ff8445
msgid "``s`` for **squash** will combine the commit with the previous commit.  In the example above \"AP_HAL_F4Light: fixed some support scripts\" and \"AP_HAL_F4LIGHT: small fix (NFC)\" will be \"squashed\" together into a single commit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-interactive-rebase.rst:34
#: f7367e6df0b444f3b076ce2f23506902
msgid "``r`` for **reword** allows you to change the subject and description of the commit.  Note that you cannot simply modify the subject line in the viewer.  First you mark it with ``r`` and later git will pop up another view to allow you to modify the subject and description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-interactive-rebase.rst:35
#: 08d7afd90a4a4cc596e4aca6cc49edd2
msgid "``e`` for **edit** allows you to modify what is in the commit (i.e. add or take away changes)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-interactive-rebase.rst:36
#: 9365496126de46cb9ad85b8f277cb037
msgid "``d`` will remove the commit, alternatively you can just delete the line from the viewer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-interactive-rebase.rst:37
#: be799ff08ae1447fac19d5f5df9702dd
msgid "you may also move lines up or down to re-order the commits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-interactive-rebase.rst:39
#: 02d271e05c084e5fbdaf00cfed8bc6d2
msgid "save and exit the viewer.  git will run through the file from top to bottom and pause when required to allow you to make the changes you have requested."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-interactive-rebase.rst:41
#: fece1f9e691444bf92f548c6bc7f6b16
msgid "if a commit was marked with ``s`` for **squash**, another viewer will pop-up to ask you to provide the commit message and subject line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-interactive-rebase.rst:45
#: 6dfe26b1b2874a7284a773cb83403685
msgid "if a commit was marked with ``e`` for **edit**, the viewer will return to the regular command line. Edit the files as you wish, commit the changes and then type ``git rebase --continue`` to allow git to continue processing the other changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-interactive-rebase.rst:50
#: 3a775ff1c76e49a6b83eb4aaa17c7ef4
msgid "When things go wrong"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-interactive-rebase.rst:52
#: bc874a0df82b4e92952467638c86c31a
msgid "If you change the order of commits or edit their contents merge conflicts may occur.  If you can resolve these with a merge tool (like `TortoiseMerge <https://tortoisegit.org/>`__) then you can allow the interactive rebase to continue by typing:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-interactive-rebase.rst:59
#: efb40c6d8b284c2cb88b6119bf366537
msgid "alternatively you may wish to abort the interactive rebase which will return your branch to its original condition before the interactive rebase was begun"
msgstr ""
